Main Lesson:

Diffie-Hellman is secure only if the private values stay private. In this challenge, the client secret b was leaked, so the shared secret could be rebuilt.

Also, the encryption used only shared % 256, meaning the final XOR key was just one byte. Once the shared secret was calculated, decrypting the flag was simple.
